<div class="bb-quote"><b>TheSoundOfTrees wrote:</b><br /><blockquote class="bb-quote-body">The &quot;Crisis&quot; storyline, at first, was decided because there were too many alternate earths and times - the story&#39;s universe was getting out of hand, it was better to write an end to it and &quot;restart&quot; with something cleaner. Some characters had 3 or 4 alternate origin stories...
&nbsp;
</blockquote></div>
I think the difference is that SotM was always -- purposefully -- building to this point. &quot;Crisis&quot; was just a response to the bloated situation.&nbsp;

[/quote]

Of course. But I think the Event, like the whole game, is an hommage to this kind of things happening in &quot;real&quot; comic books. Crisis, Civil War, House of M, all these &quot;big&quot; events that &quot;change&quot; at least temporarily the way the universe of the comic book line works.

Of course, in the &quot;real world&quot; these events have many reasons : the whim of an author or lead, the necessity to clean the line, a fall in sales leading to desperate measures or in &quot;writing out&quot; heroes that don&#39;t sell much, etc. GtG do this on purpose, and with a lot of preparation - but they do it because it happens in comic books.

In the end, the status quo won&#39;t change much : a handful of characters lost or changed mainly. The big big change is the loss of &quot;alternate&quot; timelines and universe, the limitation on planar travel, and the importance of Oblivion Shards. I am very curious to see what kind of story lines we will have in future products...

[quote="Arcanist Lupus"]

Akash&#39;Bhuta is a perfect example of what I mean. &nbsp;First there&#39;s Akash&#39;Bhuta, and then Akash&#39;Thriya working with the heroes, and then Akash&#39;Darsha, who is villainous again, but different from before.

[/quote]

&nbsp;

In her case she literally is a different type of being.

&nbsp;

Akash&#39;Bhuta is the manifestation of the earth after amassing X energy over the course of centuries. She then fights the Argent Adept and generally is defeated and the cycle begins anew.

&nbsp;

Akash&#39;Thriya is a desperate re-manisfestation in response to OblivAeon, she was only defeated a short while ago, she doesn&#39;t have enough strength to fully remanisfest. In addition, her goal is protection instead of devastation and recreation, which is a complete different goal than the spirit of Akash&#39; generally has. Also Akash&#39;Thriya is defeated and then takes power from the Void, changing her further.

&nbsp;

This taking of power from the Void and a run in with the Oblivion Shards is what creates Akash&#39;Darsha. She realized she can gather power more quickly through these methods than her normal methods and the shards have begun changing her. For example, while she has a giant manisfestation as Akash&#39;Darsha, she also has Avatars more similiar to Akash&#39;Thriya which she can send out to act seperately from herself. She is not the same being she was, she is more active, more violent, less stable, and her goals may be more gathering power than destruction and recreation, as she has realized the allure of power and what it can do for her.

&nbsp;

